{"path":"experimental/fs/hard_link_count","title":"std::experimental::filesystem::hard_link_count","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::filesystem::</span>hard_link_count","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/fs/hard_link_count","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Returns the number of hard links for the filesystem object identified by path p.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/filesystem\">&lt;experimental/filesystem&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-fs_ts\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw139\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uintmax_t</span></span></a> hard_link_count<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/integer\"><span class=\"kw139\">std::<span class=\"me2\">uintmax_t</span></span></a> hard_link_count<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> path<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> p, error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-fs-ts t-mark-ts\">(filesystem TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns the number of hard links for the filesystem object identified by path <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code>.\n</p><p>The non-throwing overload returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">static_cast</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>uintmax_t<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> on errors.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> p\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> path to examine\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ec\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> out-parameter for error reporting in the non-throwing overload\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>The number of hard links for <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\nThe overload that does not take an <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> parameter throws <a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/filesystem_error\">filesystem_error</a> on underlying OS API errors, constructed with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">p</span></code> as the first argument and the OS error code as the error code argument. <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/memory/new/bad_alloc\"><span class=\"kw698\">std::<span class=\"me2\">bad_alloc</span></span></a></span></code> may be thrown if memory allocation fails. The overload taking an <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span></span></code> parameter sets it to the OS API error code if an OS API call fails, and executes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ec.<span class=\"me1\">clear</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> if no errors occur. This overload has <div class=\"t-noexcept-inline\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/language/noexcept_spec\"><code>noexcept</code></a> specification:&nbsp;&nbsp;<div class=\"t-noexcept-box\"><span class=\"t-cc\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span></span></span></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</div>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;experimental/filesystem&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> fs <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">experimental</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">filesystem</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// On a POSIX-style filesystem, each directory has at least 2 hard links:</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// itself and the special member pathname \".\"</span>\n    fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">path</span> p <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">current_path</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Number of hard links for current path is \"</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">hard_link_count</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// each \"..\" is a hard link to the parent directory, so the total number</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// of hard links for any directory is 2 plus number of direct subdirectories</span>\n    p <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">current_path</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"..\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// each dot-dot is a hard link to parent</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Number of hard links for .. is \"</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> fs<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">hard_link_count</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Number of hard links for current path is 2\nNumber of hard links for .. is 3</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/create_hard_link\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>create_hard_link</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  creates a hard link <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/fs","title":"Filesystem library"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::filesystem::hard_link_count","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Returns the number of hard links for the filesystem object identified by path p."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"p, ec"},{"label":"Return value","note":"The number of hard links for p."},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"The overload that does not take an"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"create_hard_link","note":"creates a hard link"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":277,"codeBlockCount":2}
